# Rank 1615 / CVE-2022-1812: Publify stored the user display name
# with no length bound -- the column is a text type, so a profile
# edit could persist megabytes into the name that renders on every
# page, feed and session the user touches (unbounded input to
# resource exhaustion and cookie/session breakage, CWE-400/CWE-20;
# the huntr bounty fixed by the length validation). The User model
# in publify_core/app/models/user.rb validated the name's presence
# but never its length. the fixing commit 29a5837c29 is the fixing change
# (the advisory links this exact commit, "Validate
# length of user's name attribute"): `validates :name, length: {
# maximum: 2048 }` -- generous for any real name, bounded for the
# column semantics.g
# resolves as an umbrella layout: publify/publify contains
# publify_core as a directory, and the pool row's repository holds
# the commit the advisory names).

#
# ATTENTION, model-level length budgets. The unbounded attribute is
# a storage/render exhaustion vector and no rule can ask "does every
# user-editable attribute carry a length validation against its
# column semantics" -- Rails model validation vocabulary. The
# corpus's size-budget rules judge parser loops, not ORM attribute
# declarations. A binding on Publify's own User model would detect
# this application rather than the weakness. Measured on the real
# code: scanning user.rb reports zero findings at both revisions.
# No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change shipped. Spec
# cve_rank1615 records the unvalidated name and the length-bounded
# form, both asserting reject VYQL-DOS-029: when attribute-budget
# vocabulary lands, the unvalidated form must flip to expect.

test "rank1615: the display name has no length bound"
  lang ruby
  file publify_core/app/models/user.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  class User < ActiveRecord::Base
    validates :name, presence: true
    validates :login, presence: true, uniqueness: true
    validates :email, presence: true, uniqueness: true

    def display_name
      name
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1615: the fixed revision bounds the name length"
  lang ruby
  file publify_core/app/models/user.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  class User < ActiveRecord::Base
    validates :name, presence: true
    validates :name, length: { maximum: 2048 }
    validates :login, presence: true, uniqueness: true
    validates :email, presence: true, uniqueness: true

    def display_name
      name
    end
  end
  ```
